# A comma inside a parenthesized right table (M1-19).
mode: syntax
---- query
from T | join (from U | where a, b) on k
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..41
  PIPELINE@0..40
    IDENT@0..4 "from"
    WHITESPACE@4..5 " "
    NAME_REF@5..6
      IDENT@5..6 "T"
    WHITESPACE@6..7 " "
    PIPE@7..8 "|"
    WHITESPACE@8..9 " "
    JOIN_OP@9..40
      IDENT@9..13 "join"
      WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
      PAREN_EXPR@14..35
        L_PAREN@14..15 "("
        PIPELINE@15..34
          IDENT@15..19 "from"
          WHITESPACE@19..20 " "
          NAME_REF@20..21
            IDENT@20..21 "U"
          WHITESPACE@21..22 " "
          PIPE@22..23 "|"
          WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
          WHERE_OP@24..34
            IDENT@24..29 "where"
            WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
            NAME_REF@30..31
              IDENT@30..31 "a"
            COMMA@31..32 ","
            WHITESPACE@32..33 " "
            NAME_REF@33..34
              IDENT@33..34 "b"
        R_PAREN@34..35 ")"
      WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
      IDENT@36..38 "on"
      WHITESPACE@38..39 " "
      NAME_REF@39..40
        IDENT@39..40 "k"
  WHITESPACE@40..41 "\n"

error[DS0115]: `where` takes one condition
  --> query:1:32
  |
1 | from T | join (from U | where a, b) on k
  |                                ^ a comma does not join conditions
  |
  = help: combine the conditions with `and`: `a and b`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    from T | join (from U | where a and b) on k
which parses without errors
